sentences.l:
The Master said: “Courteous but without the rites — then toil;
careful but without the rites — then fearfulness;
brave but without the rites — then disorder;
straight but without the rites — then cutting.”

Master Zeng said: “Able, and asking of the unable;
having much, and asking of those with little;
having, as though without;
full, as though empty;
wronged, and keeping no tally —
once I had a friend who gave himself to these.”

An imperilled state, do not enter;
a disordered state, do not dwell in.
When the world has the Way, come forward;
when it lacks the Way, stay hidden.

The Master said: “Wild, yet not straight;
ignorant, yet not careful;
witless, yet without good faith —
I do not know what to make of them.”

The Master said: “Yu — I find no gap in him.
Meagre in drink and food, yet full in filial devotion to the spirits and gods;
poor in clothes and garments, yet full in the beauty of his apron and cap;
low in house and rooms, yet giving his whole strength to the ditches and channels.
Yu — I find no gap in him.”
